<llsd>
  <array>

    <!-- <Lumen> ONLY Lumen.

         Firestorm's skins shipped here for no better reason than that a fork
         inherits everything: AnsaStorm, MetaHarper, StarLight, StarLight CUI,
         Vintage, and one named "Firestorm" itself. Most were made by individual
         people in that community FOR Firestorm, and redistributing their work
         inside a different viewer is not something any of them agreed to.

         The author put it better than "courtesy", which is what this had been
         called: *"i stedet for tager noget af deres og sender med vores"*.

         Measured before deciding, and the measurement settles it: no other fork
         does this. Megapahit ships classic, contrast and gold; Alchemy ships
         alchemy, heretic and ionic; both their own. Linden Lab's viewer offers
         none at all. Lumen was the only one carrying somebody else's set.

         `default` stays on disk because every skin layers over it, but it is
         not offered here and never was. Removing the other six takes 69 MB out
         of the bundle, which is the smallest of the reasons. -->

    <map>
      <key>name</key>
      <string>Lumen</string>
      <key>folder</key>
      <string>lumen</string>

      <!-- <Lumen> One look, not five. The inherited colour schemes were
           Firestorm's, credited to their individual authors, and re-offering
           them under this skin's name was neither useful nor quite honest.
           High Contrast was kept for a while as an accessibility feature and
           has now gone too, on the author's instruction: it was Firestorm's
           High Contrast, not a Lumen one, and shipping a second scheme nobody
           designed for this skin is not accessibility. If Lumen needs a high
           contrast mode it should have one built for it. -->
      <key>themes</key>
      <array>
        <map>
          <key>name</key>
          <string>Lumen</string>
          <key>folder</key>
          <string/>
        </map>
      </array>
    </map>

  </array>
</llsd>
